@page "/"

<PageTitle>Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">shadcn/ui for Blazor static SSR</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    The same tokens, the same class strings, the same <code>data-slot</code> on every root, the
    same ARIA. Write the shadcn markup you already know; the translation is four rules long.
</p>

<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <Button Href="/components/button">Browse components</Button>
    <Button Variant="outline" Href="/blocks">Blocks</Button>
    <Button Variant="outline" Href="/theming">Theming</Button>
</div>

<h2 class="doc-h2">React to Razor</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Parameters are PascalCase; HTML attributes stay lowercase and are splatted onto the root.
    That splat is the whole Unpoly integration — no component here knows Unpoly exists.
</p>

<div class="doc-example">
    <pre class="doc-source"><code>&lt;Button variant="destructive" size="sm"&gt;    →  &lt;Button Variant="destructive" Size="sm"&gt;
className="w-full"                          →  Class="w-full"
&lt;Button asChild&gt;&lt;Link href="/x"&gt;           →  &lt;Button Href="/x"&gt;
&lt;Input name="email" value={v} /&gt;            →  &lt;Input name="email" value="@@v" /&gt;
onClick={...}                               →  there are none — a form posts, a link navigates
cn(...) resolves conflicts                  →  it does here too: ClassMerge is tailwind-merge</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="doc-h2">What it is built on</h2>

<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <Card>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle Class="text-base">The platform, first</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            Dialog is <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>. Accordion is <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>.
            Menus and tooltips are <code>[popover]</code>. Select is a real
            <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> that posts without JavaScript. The focus trap, the
            top layer and Escape are the browser's.
        </CardContent>
    </Card>

    <Card>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Parity you can check</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            Class lists are generated from shadcn's own source and compared against it by the
            tests. Every difference is in <code>deviations.json</code> with a written reason.
        </CardContent>
    </Card>

    <Card>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Unpoly, by attribute</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <code>up-target</code>, <code>up-poll</code>, <code>up-validate</code>,
            <code>up-disable</code> are written as plain HTML at the call site. The one point of
            contact is a CSS rule: a button that started a request grows a spinner.
        </CardContent>
    </Card>
</div>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Try the switcher</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The theme control in the header changes <code>data-theme</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>
    and nothing else. Every component on this page is the same markup under all four.
</p>

